WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:02.768
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:02.901 --> 00:06.523
Let's build and download a gene panel.

00:06.867 --> 00:11.059
How do you get a gene panel
from SysNDD that you can cite?

00:11.192 --> 00:15.587
Four parts: filter, check, export and cite.

00:15.933 --> 00:21.053
In the top bar,
open the Tables menu, then select Panels.

00:21.400 --> 00:23.882
The page is called Panel compilation.

00:24.015 --> 00:28.169
Each row is one gene, not one entity.

00:28.533 --> 00:31.262
SysNDD grades entities.

00:31.396 --> 00:36.107
An entity links a gene,
a mode of inheritance and a disease.

00:36.241 --> 00:38.046
A panel lists genes.

00:38.180 --> 00:42.417
It files each gene under
the highest category of its entities.

00:42.551 --> 00:46.787
<i>FBXO11</i> has a Definitive and a Refuted entity,

00:46.921 --> 00:49.536
so the panel lists it under Definitive.

00:49.670 --> 00:53.096
Only entities marked NDD Yes count:

00:53.230 --> 00:56.933
their disease is a neurodevelopmental disorder.

00:57.300 --> 01:00.246
In Category, choose Definitive.

01:00.379 --> 01:05.815
The table now lists every gene
whose highest entity is Definitive.

01:06.167 --> 01:11.212
Leave Inheritance at All
to keep every mode of inheritance.

01:11.345 --> 01:16.473
Beside the title,
the Genes count shows the size of your panel.

01:16.833 --> 01:21.934
A mode of inheritance belongs
to each entity, not to the gene.

01:22.068 --> 01:27.842
<i>FBXO11</i> has two NDD entities:
a Definitive dominant entity

01:27.976 --> 01:30.656
and a Refuted recessive one.

01:30.790 --> 01:34.147
Only the dominant entity is Definitive.

01:34.281 --> 01:37.659
So before you filter variants by mode of inheritance,

01:37.793 --> 01:42.752
open the gene page and see which
entity carries which category.

01:43.100 --> 01:48.172
Back on the Panels page, select the .xlsx button.

01:48.533 --> 01:53.893
It downloads the whole panel,
every page, as one Excel file.

01:54.233 --> 01:56.461
The file has three sheets.

01:56.595 --> 02:00.638
The data sheet has one row per gene,
with gene identifiers

02:00.772 --> 02:05.886
and coordinates on hg19 and hg38.

02:06.020 --> 02:09.742
The meta sheet records the query that built the panel.

02:09.876 --> 02:11.906
Keep it with your analysis.

02:12.040 --> 02:16.794
The links sheet records the query as an API address.

02:17.167 --> 02:21.917
Write down the download date,
because the file does not record it.

02:22.050 --> 02:29.050
Under the SysNDD name in the top bar,
you see the version, here 0.38.2.

02:30.733 --> 02:33.751
Under Help, About, open Citation Policy.

02:33.885 --> 02:37.679
The Primary Citation names the SysNDD paper.

02:37.813 --> 02:41.007
Cite it whenever you use SysNDD.

02:41.367 --> 02:47.273
In your methods, name the panel,
the SysNDD version and your access date.

02:47.406 --> 02:52.048
Curators keep entities up to date,
so the version and the date tell readers

02:52.181 --> 02:56.408
which state of SysNDD you used.

02:56.767 --> 02:59.907
Remember: a panel files each gene under

03:00.040 --> 03:04.185
the highest category of its NDD entities.

03:04.318 --> 03:07.641
A mode of inheritance belongs to each entity,

03:07.774 --> 03:12.952
so check the gene page before you
filter variants by mode of inheritance.

03:13.085 --> 03:17.915
Finally, cite the SysNDD
paper with the version and date,

03:18.048 --> 03:21.567
and keep the meta sheet with your analysis.

03:21.933 --> 03:28.493
The documentation chapter
Build and download a gene panel shows every step.
